<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="c0db2e2b">&lt;p&gt;
    Test execution&amp;nbsp;is executed based&amp;nbsp;on&amp;nbsp;a defined schedule that dictates frequency,&amp;nbsp;sequence, data and
    the appropriate environment to use when executing tests. For manually executed tests, specific instructions detailed in
    test cases are followed step by step. Test scripts used in automated testing execute specific instructions written in a
    computer programming language.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="b3d4825d"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="538bb129"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="b2b49ef3"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="81988982">&lt;p&gt;
    To validate that the entire system, including integrations and interfaces&amp;nbsp;with external systems, works&amp;nbsp;as
    intended and to document where it does not (test failure).
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
